{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-adelic-substrate","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:adelic-substrate","kind":"definition","title":"Adelic substrate $\\mathbb{A}$","cites":["references/tate1967"],"tags":["adeles","macroscopic-limit","global","non-archimedean"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.AdelicSubstrate","text":"adelic-substrate.md","leanSource":"adelic-substrate.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:adelic-substrate\"></a><p><em>The <strong>adelic substrate</strong> of the QOU framework is the ring of adeles of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Q}</code>,</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathbb{A}\n  \\;=\\;\n  \\mathbb{R} \\;\\times\\; \\prod_{p}{}^{\\!\\!\\prime}\\;\\mathbb{Q}_p,</code></pre>\n<p><em>the restricted product of the archimedean completion <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{R}</code> with all <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code>-adic completions <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Q}_p</code> (restriction: almost all components lie in the maximal compact subring <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Z}_p</code>).</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/adelic-substrate.md","heading":"Definition","number":"13.4.56","page":"b/def-adelic-substrate","qa":{"counts":{"pass":79,"fail":1,"warn":1,"na":11,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BringsSurface.AdelicSubstrate","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/adelic-substrate.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
